From 5de6fe71ce153dce28ebe9be044d0b38a9531608 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mira <mira@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 20:34:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] (thirdparty) ck-phdr-unwind jemalloc with libunwind
 backtracer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Pass `--enable-prof-libunwind` to `build_jemalloc_doris()` so jemalloc's
heap-profile backtracer calls `unw_backtrace` instead of libgcc's
`_Unwind_Backtrace`. The libgcc path re-enters `dl_iterate_phdr` through
`_Unwind_Find_FDE` and deadlocks against the lock-free override under
profiling load.

Detection inputs (CPPFLAGS/LDFLAGS/LIBS) are supplied by the caller's
environment rather than hard-coded here, so the patch stays minimal and
the harness wrapper (scripts/phase2/phase2-jemalloc.sh) keeps the
rebuild-scenario plumbing in one place.

Add a post-configure verify of `result: prof-libunwind : 1` in
`config.log` and fail early on mismatch. jemalloc/jemalloc#2504:
detection can silently fall back to libgcc; without the verify the
build would succeed and quietly produce a libgcc-backed archive.

In a fully-clean `build-thirdparty.sh` run, libunwind is built later in
the package list than jemalloc, so a clean invocation of this function
will not yet see libunwind and the verify will fail. The intended
invocation is `build-thirdparty.sh jemalloc_doris` after the prebuilt
thirdparty (which includes libunwind) is in place — i.e. the rebuild
scenario the ck-phdr-unwind variant exercises.

Spec: docs/design/ck.md "Decisions".

Co-Authored-By: jover <joverzh@gmail.com>
---
 thirdparty/build-thirdparty.sh | 18 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/thirdparty/build-thirdparty.sh b/thirdparty/build-thirdparty.sh
index 71a3b38afb8..673a0ddde92 100755
--- a/thirdparty/build-thirdparty.sh
+++ b/thirdparty/build-thirdparty.sh
@@ -1613,8 +1613,24 @@ build_jemalloc_doris() {
     # It is not easy to remove `with-jemalloc-prefix`, which may affect the compatibility between third-party and old version codes.
     # Also, will building failed on Mac, it said can't find mallctl symbol. because jemalloc's default prefix on macOS is "je_", not "".
     # Maybe can use alias instead of overwrite.
+    # Reason: `--enable-prof-libunwind` makes jemalloc's heap-profile
+    # backtracer call `unw_backtrace`. The default libgcc backtracer
+    # re-enters `dl_iterate_phdr` and deadlocks against the lock-free
+    # override (be/src/common/phdr_cache.cpp) under profiling load.
+    # `CPPFLAGS`/`LDFLAGS`/`LIBS` for libunwind detection come from the
+    # caller's env (see scripts/phase2/phase2-jemalloc.sh).
+    # Spec: docs/design/ck.md "Decisions".
     CFLAGS="${cflags}" ../configure --prefix="${TP_INSTALL_DIR}" --with-install-suffix="_doris" "${WITH_LG_PAGE}" \
-        --with-jemalloc-prefix=je --enable-prof --disable-cxx --disable-libdl --disable-shared
+        --with-jemalloc-prefix=je --enable-prof --enable-prof-libunwind \
+        --disable-cxx --disable-libdl --disable-shared
+
+    # Reason: libunwind detection can silently fall back to libgcc
+    # (jemalloc/jemalloc#2504). Fail before sinking time into `make`.
+    if ! grep -qE "result: prof-libunwind +: 1$" config.log; then
+        echo "ERROR: prof-libunwind != 1 in config.log; libunwind detection failed (jemalloc/jemalloc#2504)." >&2
+        grep -E "result: prof-(libunwind|libgcc|gcc) +:" config.log >&2 || true
+        exit 1
+    fi
 
     make -j "${PARALLEL}"
     make install
